# Coach speech (Arabic, Modern Standard Arabic): the appraisal after the game
# (src/coach/appraisal.cpp). Same keys and variants as assets/coach/speech/en/appraisal.lang; its
# header documents every placeholder. Always positive, never blaming.
#
# Register (as common.lang and review.lang): second person singular, gender-neutral where the
# writing allows ("الفوز لك", "كان الفوز في يدك", "كانت لديك", "لم ترتكب", "استرجعنا"). A
# 2nd-person past verb is also the coach's "I": "فزت / لعبت / وجدت" are avoided; "أخذت ... من
# قطعي" and "هزمتني" are kept because the coach cannot be their subject. The coach's own figures
# are nouns ("دقتي", "الفوز لي").
# Move numbers are said as cardinals after the noun ("في النقلة {n}" = في النقلة سبعة), as in the
# opening texts ("خرجنا من النظرية المعروفة في النقلة {n}").
# Counts: "{moves:move}", "{n:piece}", "{m:time}", "{n:mistake}", "{m:f}" (a feminine number,
# نقلة understood: "في ثلاث منها") ...; a dual count is oblique, so every count follows a verb, a
# preposition (مع، في، من، سوى) or a verbal noun ("أخذ {n:piece}", "استرجاع {n:move}").
# {opening:def} is the definite opening name of assets/coach/openings/ar.lang ("الدفاع الصقلي").

